{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43464 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- is consistently identified as a target of multiple entities, including HaCaT, Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, and Carboxylesterase 2, all of which are implicated in the regulation of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. This suggests a potential mechanism by which Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- may influence the activity of Replicase polyprotein 1ab through the modulation of downstream targets. The evidence points to a possible pathway where Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- acts as a regulator of cellular processes that ultimately affect the function of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The shared involvement of these targets in the regulation of Replicase polyprotein 1ab implies a possible dependency on these pathways, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these findings highlights the potential for Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- to exert its effects through a network of molecular interactions that ultimately modulate the activity of Replicase polyprotein 1ab.",
